---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';

const updated = '2026-05-23';
---

<Base
  title={`Privacy — ${SITE.name}`}
  description={`How ${SITE.name} handles your data.`}
>
  <section class="container-wide py-20">
    <div class="kicker">// privacy</div>
    <h1 class="mt-3 font-display text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-white md:text-6xl">
      Privacy
    </h1>
    <p class="ui-text mt-3">// last updated {updated}</p>

    <div class="prose-frontier mt-10">
      <p>
        SmartXChain is built to be privacy-friendly by default. We don't run
        third-party advertising, we don't use cookies for tracking, and we
        don't sell or rent your data.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>

      <h3>Newsletter subscribers</h3>
      <p>
        If you subscribe to <em>{SITE.newsletter.name}</em>, your email address
        is stored at our newsletter provider, <a href="https://buttondown.email/about/privacy">Buttondown</a>.
        Buttondown is the data processor; SmartXChain is the controller. We
        only use your email to send the newsletter you signed up for. Every
        email contains an unsubscribe link. Unsubscribing removes you from
        the list immediately and permanently.
      </p>

      <h3>Analytics</h3>
      <p>
        We use <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/">Cloudflare
        Web Analytics</a> to understand which articles are read. It is
        cookie-less, privacy-friendly, and does not track individual visitors
        across sessions or sites. It collects only aggregated, anonymized
        page-view counts.
      </p>

      <h3>Logs</h3>
      <p>
        Cloudflare, our hosting provider, retains standard request logs (IP
        address, timestamp, user agent) for a short period for security and
        abuse-prevention purposes. We do not access or use these logs for any
        editorial or marketing purpose.
      </p>

      <h2>What we don't do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>We don't use tracking cookies.</li>
        <li>We don't run third-party ad networks.</li>
        <li>We don't share your email with anyone outside Buttondown.</li>
        <li>We don't fingerprint visitors.</li>
        <li>We don't have a cookie banner because we don't need one.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        You can unsubscribe from the newsletter at any time using the link in
        every issue. If you'd like your data removed from Buttondown entirely,
        email us at <a href="mailto:hectorg@smartxchain.com">hectorg@smartxchain.com</a>
        and we'll handle it.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We'll update this page if our practices change. The "last updated"
        date above tells you when. Material changes get announced in the
        newsletter.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
